# Odin III's Phase 3 script up to, but not including, `abc` (3G WR-9, 3C spec H-2): the single
# source of the string hardmap-diff runs. `wreduce` runs before `flatten` as in Parmys; `hardmap`
# needs the flat design; the last `opt -full -ffbits` also merges the identical bits of word
# flip-flops, which Yosys merges after techmap (PHASE3 #49); `lower` makes the netlist view;
# `compact` renumbers IDs last.
# @ADDERLIB@ is the n-bit soft adder Parmys gets from vtr_primitives.v (spec A-9; dropped when
# the tool has none). @LIB@ is lib/vtr.o3lib, @DESIGN@ the source, @OUT@ the BLIF hardmap-diff compares to Parmys's.
read_techlib @LIB@
read_verilog --lib @ADDERLIB@
read_verilog --nolatches --vtr-compat @DESIGN@
proc
opt
wreduce
opt_clean
opt -full
flatten
opt -full
hardmap
opt -full -ffbits
lower
opt -fast
compact
write_blif --vtr @OUT@
